/-!
# Framework.Homological

CSS codes as length-3 chain complexes over `ZMod 2`, and bivariate bicycle
codes.

Chain complexes and their codes:

- `Code`: `HomologicalCode`, a chain complex `C₂ → C₁ → C₀` with its cycles,
  boundaries, homology `H1` and the dual complex.
- `CSS`: the X-type and Z-type Pauli operators of a 1-chain, and the X- and
  Z-support chains of a Pauli group element.
- `Generators`: the face and vertex stabilizers, and commutation of chain
  operators through the pairing of 1-chains.
- `StabGroup`: the stabilizer group generated by the checks.
- `LogicalCorrespondence`: chain operators are logical exactly on (dual)
  cycles and trivial exactly on (dual) boundaries.
- `Distance`: the code distance from the weights of the nontrivial cycles and
  dual cycles.
- `Presentation`: the `StabilizerCode.Presentation` of a complex whose checks
  are independent.
- `ToCode`: the `StabilizerCode` of an arbitrary complex, with `dim H₁` logical
  qubits.
- `SelfDual`: the complex of a self-orthogonal binary check matrix, which is
  its own dual.
- `SelfDualLogical`: the single logical class of such a code on `2 |F| + 1`
  qubits with `|F|` independent checks.
- `LiftedProduct`: the 1×2 lifted product over the group algebra of a
  possibly non-abelian group.

Bivariate bicycle codes:

- `BBChainComplex`: convolution on `G → ZMod 2` and the chain complex
  `bbChainComplex A B`.
- `BBLogicalQubits`: `dim H₁ = 2 · dim (ker A ⊓ ker B)`.
- `BBStabilizerCode`: the code `bbStabilizerCode ℓ m A B` over
  `ZMod ℓ × ZMod m`.
- `BBDuality`: the dual of the complex of `(A, B)` is the complex of the
  reflected pair, by a weight-preserving involution.
- `BBConvRing`: convolution is the product of the group algebra
  `AddMonoidAlgebra (ZMod 2) G`.
- `BBSmallCycle`: a finite criterion for every nonzero cycle to have weight at
  least 6.

Double covers of bivariate bicycle codes:

- `Covering`: pushforward and pullback of chains along a map, a group
  homomorphism and a double cover.
- `BBCover`: `XDoubleCoverData`, a free double cover with its transfer maps,
  sheets and seam chains.
- `BBDoubling`: the doubling theorem, the distance of the cover is twice the
  distance of the base under floor hypotheses on the base.
- `BBDeficitWall`: the base chains whose pullback is a boundary are the seam
  cosets; parity of the floors.
- `BBFlatLift`: the cover cycles over a flat cover boundary.
- `BBTransferH1`: the transfer maps on `H₁`, the deck endomorphism `ε_*` and
  the criterion `BocksteinVanishes`.
- `BBBocksteinRank`: the rank of `τ ∘ p` for an exact pair of linear maps.
- `BBDeckTower`: if the deck translation acts trivially on `H₁` then `1 + σ`
  lies in the ideal `(A, B)`.
- `BBEpsFree`: the annihilator condition `EpsFree` for chain rings and free
  extensions.
- `BBEpsFreeGroupAlgebra`: `EpsFree` for the deck element of a group algebra.
- `BocksteinLift`: the composite of the two connecting maps vanishes on
  representatives, over a ring in which the annihilator of `ε` is `(ε ^ 3)`.
- `BBBocksteinTransport`: `BocksteinVanishes` when the deck translation lifts
  to an element of order four.

Kernel-checked certificates:

- `F2Mask`: chains packed into `Nat` bitmasks.
- `BZCertificate`: Brouwer–Zimmermann certificates for weight floors of binary
  linear codes.
- `BBSeamBZ`: such certificates for the seam-coset floor and the light
  boundaries of a double cover.
- `Certificate`: soundness lemmas for packed-`Nat` certificate checks.
-/
